From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] kernelbase, conhost: console command history per program

GetConsoleCommandHistory(Length)A/W, ExpungeConsoleCommandHistoryA/W, SetConsoleNumberOfCommandsA/W
and Get/SetConsoleHistoryInfo were stubs or missing (pywin32 binds them: NVDA, Anki). As Windows'
console host does: one history per executable name (4 by default, 50 commands each, the least
recently used one taken over), the line ReadConsole reads goes to the reader's history (ReadConsole
names it: the console input exe name, which now starts as the program's file name as on Windows),
HISTORY_NO_DUP_FLAG moves a repeated command last. Sizes in bytes (W) and characters (A); a buffer too
small gives ERROR_BUFFER_OVERFLOW. Gate: test/conhist-gate.sh. Mutants: SG_MUTANT_NO_READ_EXE,
SG_MUTANT_ONE_HISTORY.
